From 12d407f488bf02563015406e07645e588a2d8841 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:20:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add droid camera HAL and notifier plugins for Halium devices

On Halium devices the cameras sit behind the Android camera HAL and no
/dev/video capture nodes exist, so the v4l2 HAL plugin and the PDM
notifier never find anything and getCameraList stays empty.

hal-droid implements IHal over a gst-droid pipeline (droidcamsrc raw
NV21 viewfinder into an appsink); frames are copied into the service's
buffers per getBuffer and flow into the normal shared-memory
distribution. notifier-droid probes the droid camera count through
droidcamsrc's clamped camera-device property range and announces
builtin devices with droid:<n> device nodes mapped to the droid
subsystem. Both plugins no-op cleanly when gst-droid is not installed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS Halium-specific]
